IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ec-act`

-- Executive Condominium Housing Scheme Act 1996 -- worked cases.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN `owned` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `sold within 30 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `misrepresented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Applicant
DECIDE `an applicant who` `owned` `sold within 30 months` `misrepresented` IS
    Applicant WITH
        `name` IS "A"
        `the person or spouse owned or purchased property between application and the temporary occupation permit` IS `owned`
        `the person or spouse sold or divested property within 30 months before the application` IS `sold within 30 months`
        `the person or spouse sold or divested property between application and the temporary occupation permit` IS FALSE
        `the person or spouse made a misrepresentation of material fact or a false statement in a material particular relating to the purchase` IS `misrepresented`
        `the person or spouse became ineligible under regulations made under section 3(2) between application and the permit` IS FALSE
        `the property concerned is commercial property acquired with the Minister's prior written consent` IS FALSE
        `the value of that commercial property at the time of purchase in dollars` IS 0
        `the Minister has allowed a higher value than $250,000` IS FALSE

`a clean applicant` MEANS `an applicant who` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `5(1) -- the four disqualifying grounds`

#ASSERT NOT `the person is not entitled to purchase under section 5(1)` `a clean applicant`
#ASSERT `the person is not entitled to purchase under section 5(1)` (`an applicant who` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is not entitled to purchase under section 5(1)` (`an applicant who` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is not entitled to purchase under section 5(1)` (`an applicant who` FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- s 5(2) follows from s 5(1) and nothing else.
#ASSERT `the purchaser must not present the assurance for registration` (`an applicant who` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the purchaser must not present the assurance for registration` `a clean applicant`

-- LIMB (c) HAS NO TIME WINDOW AND NO MENTAL ELEMENT. (a), (b) and (d) are each
-- confined to a stated period; (c) is "has at any time ... made any
-- misrepresentation of a material fact or false statement in a material
-- particular, WHETHER INNOCENTLY OR OTHERWISE". So an honest mistake, whenever
-- made, disqualifies. The assertion above on the third applicant is that case:
-- the only true fact about them is an innocent misstatement.

§§ `5(9) -- the commercial property saving, and its cap`

GIVEN `value` IS A NUMBER, `higher allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Applicant
DECIDE `an owner of commercial property worth` `value` `higher allowed` IS
    Applicant WITH
        `name` IS "B"
        `the person or spouse owned or purchased property between application and the temporary occupation permit` IS TRUE
        `the person or spouse sold or divested property within 30 months before the application` IS FALSE
        `the person or spouse sold or divested property between application and the temporary occupation permit` IS FALSE
        `the person or spouse made a misrepresentation of material fact or a false statement in a material particular relating to the purchase` IS FALSE
        `the person or spouse became ineligible under regulations made under section 3(2) between application and the permit` IS FALSE
        `the property concerned is commercial property acquired with the Minister's prior written consent` IS TRUE
        `the value of that commercial property at the time of purchase in dollars` IS `value`
        `the Minister has allowed a higher value than $250,000` IS `higher allowed`

-- "not exceeding $250,000": the cap itself is inside the saving.
#ASSERT `the section 5(9) saving applies` (`an owner of commercial property worth` 250000 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the section 5(9) saving applies` (`an owner of commercial property worth` 250001 FALSE)
#ASSERT `the section 5(9) saving applies` (`an owner of commercial property worth` 400000 TRUE)

-- The saving is what decides entitlement for an owner of commercial property.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is not entitled to purchase under section 5(1)` (`an owner of commercial property worth` 250000 FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is not entitled to purchase under section 5(1)` (`an owner of commercial property worth` 250001 FALSE)

-- Without the Minister's prior written consent the saving does not apply, however
-- small the value.
`a consentless owner of a $1 shop` MEANS Applicant WITH
    `name` IS "C"
    `the person or spouse owned or purchased property between application and the temporary occupation permit` IS TRUE
    `the person or spouse sold or divested property within 30 months before the application` IS FALSE
    `the person or spouse sold or divested property between application and the temporary occupation permit` IS FALSE
    `the person or spouse made a misrepresentation of material fact or a false statement in a material particular relating to the purchase` IS FALSE
    `the person or spouse became ineligible under regulations made under section 3(2) between application and the permit` IS FALSE
    `the property concerned is commercial property acquired with the Minister's prior written consent` IS FALSE
    `the value of that commercial property at the time of purchase in dollars` IS 1
    `the Minister has allowed a higher value than $250,000` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the section 5(9) saving applies` `a consentless owner of a $1 shop`
#ASSERT `the person is not entitled to purchase under section 5(1)` `a consentless owner of a $1 shop`

§§ `5(3)-(5) -- the developer's duty and the appeal`

GIVEN `permit issued` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `satisfied of contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `assurance registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `appealed` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DeveloperSituation
DECIDE `a developer situation` `permit issued` `satisfied of contravention` `assurance registered` `appealed` `disposed of` IS
    DeveloperSituation WITH
        `the applicant` IS `a clean applicant`
        `the temporary occupation permit has issued` IS `permit issued`
        `the developer is satisfied of a contravention of section 5(1) or section 7(1)(a)` IS `satisfied of contravention`
        `an assurance has been registered in favour of the purchaser` IS `assurance registered`
        `the purchaser appealed to the Minister within 14 days after service` IS `appealed`
        `the appeal has been disposed of` IS `disposed of`

-- The duty arises only BEFORE the temporary occupation permit issues.
#ASSERT `the developer must serve a section 5(3) notice` (`a developer situation` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the developer must serve a section 5(3) notice` (`a developer situation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the developer must serve a section 5(3) notice` (`a developer situation` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Which notice depends on whether an assurance has been registered.
#ASSERT `the notice is one of intention to lodge a vesting instrument under section 5(3)(a)` (`a developer situation` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the notice is one of intention to terminate the agreement under section 5(3)(b)` (`a developer situation` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the notice is one of intention to terminate the agreement under section 5(3)(b)` (`a developer situation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 5(5): an appeal freezes the lodging until it is disposed of.
#ASSERT `the developer must not lodge the vesting instrument yet` (`a developer situation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the developer must not lodge the vesting instrument yet` (`a developer situation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the developer must not lodge the vesting instrument yet` (`a developer situation` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `6 -- death before the permit issues`

#ASSERT `the developer must cancel the application under section 6` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the developer must cancel the application under section 6` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the developer must cancel the application under section 6` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the amount refundable under section 6` 100000 4000 EQUALS 96000

§§ `7 -- the transfer prohibition`

GIVEN `is a transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `in the pre-permit window` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `in the minimum occupation period` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Transfer
DECIDE `a transfer that` `is a transfer` `in the pre-permit window` `in the minimum occupation period` `consented` IS
    Transfer WITH
        `a transfer of the accommodation or an estate or interest, or the creation of a trust for sale` IS `is a transfer`
        `made between the application and the issue of the temporary occupation permit` IS `in the pre-permit window`
        `made within the minimum occupation period` IS `in the minimum occupation period`
        `the Minister gave prior written consent` IS `consented`

#ASSERT `the transfer contravenes section 7(1)` (`a transfer that` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the transfer contravenes section 7(1)` (`a transfer that` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the transfer contravenes section 7(1)` (`a transfer that` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- The Minister's prior written consent lifts the prohibition in both windows.
#ASSERT NOT `the transfer contravenes section 7(1)` (`a transfer that` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the transfer contravenes section 7(1)` (`a transfer that` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- s 7(2) and s 7(3) are two consequences of one contravention: the transfer is
-- void AND the person commits an offence. Both, not either.
#ASSERT `the transfer is void under section 7(2)` (`a transfer that` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 7(3)` (`a transfer that` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `9 -- compulsory acquisition`

GIVEN `ceased to occupy` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `acquired property` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `commercial with consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN AcquisitionGrounds
DECIDE `grounds where` `ceased to occupy` `acquired property` `commercial with consent` `value` IS
    AcquisitionGrounds WITH
        `ceased to occupy within the minimum occupation period` IS `ceased to occupy`
        `acquired title to or an interest in any flat, house, building or land` IS `acquired property`
        `used otherwise than as a housing accommodation within the minimum occupation period` IS FALSE
        `assigned, underlet or parted with possession within the minimum occupation period without consent` IS FALSE
        `failed to perform a term or condition after written notice drawing attention to it` IS FALSE
        `made a misleading or false statement in the application` IS FALSE
        `made a misrepresentation of a material fact, whether innocently or otherwise` IS FALSE
        `contravened section 7(1)(b)` IS FALSE
        `ceased to be a citizen of Singapore within the minimum occupation period` IS FALSE
        `the property acquired is commercial property acquired with the Minister's prior written consent` IS `commercial with consent`
        `the value of that commercial property at the time of purchase in dollars` IS `value`
        `the Minister has allowed a higher value for this acquisition` IS FALSE

`no grounds at all` MEANS `grounds where` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0

#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may direct compulsory acquisition` `no grounds at all`
#ASSERT `the Minister may direct compulsory acquisition` (`grounds where` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT `the Minister may direct compulsory acquisition` (`grounds where` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0)

-- s 9(10) saves limb (b) on the same terms as s 5(9) saves s 5(1): commercial
-- property with consent, up to $250,000.
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(1)(b) is made out` (`grounds where` FALSE TRUE TRUE 250000)
#ASSERT `section 9(1)(b) is made out` (`grounds where` FALSE TRUE TRUE 250001)
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may direct compulsory acquisition` (`grounds where` FALSE TRUE TRUE 250000)
#ASSERT `the Minister may direct compulsory acquisition` (`grounds where` FALSE TRUE TRUE 250001)

-- The saving reaches only limb (b). Another ground stands whatever the
-- commercial property is worth.
#ASSERT `the Minister may direct compulsory acquisition` (`grounds where` TRUE TRUE TRUE 250000)
